At the application layer, I care about API contract, request semantics, authentication headers, idempotency keys, pagination, retries from clients, and protocol choice such as HTTP, gRPC, or WebSocket.



-------

Transport 

| Port | Usually used for |
| ---: | ---------------- |
|   80 | HTTP             |
|  443 | HTTPS            |
|   53 | DNS              |
|   22 | SSH              |
| 5432 | PostgreSQL       |
| 3306 | MySQL            |
| 6379 | Redis            |
| 9092 | Kafka            |


For APIs and financial systems, I would generally use TCP-based protocols because correctness and ordered delivery matter. For realtime media or latency-sensitive traffic, UDP or QUIC may be better because retransmitting old packets can hurt user experience.